From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1ma <hello@1ma.ai>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 09:54:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 1ma: a continued chat keeps a link to its source

"Continue in new chat" (the composer handoff) now sends the source thread's
id with the create request, so the new thread is stored with
sourceThreadId set and originKind null. Before, the request carried no
source at all: the only trace was a mention of the source thread in the
draft text, which the user can edit away, so plugins could not tell a
continuation from an unrelated new chat (1ma bots need this to keep the
continuation with the same bot).

Nothing is copied: history, provider session, title, attachments and the
fork point stay gated on originKind "fork". Parent, visibility and sidebar
placement do not change, and environment resolution ignores the source,
as it did before.

The server no longer rejects sourceThreadId without an originKind; the
source is still validated the same way (same project, not archived, not
deleted). The plugin SDK documents sourceThreadId with a null originKind as
"continued from".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
